{"parentUuid":"e0c0e40b-cbef-4847-aaf8-f975ea4e42ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a9f69a56-41de-4fd2-88ce-bc0e210b67cb","agentId":"aff5f77e5ff2eecdd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8tfRYmAv2gz5vohUGt1oR","type":"tool_result","content":"MISS: this textbook introduced.\nMISS: as much a matter of art, trial-and-error, and intuition, as it is of science,\nMISS: organising training according to the classical model of Matveyev can be used only by athletes of low qualification for certain phases of the programme,\nMISS: utilises only two factors,\nMISS: mainly on the example of three sports, namely swimming, weightlifting, track and field athletics.\nMISS: notorious peaks of sports form.\nMISS: was strongly influenced by the 'five year plans' and other cycles of productivity in the soviet system,\nMISS: the precise calculation of training quantities reflected attempts to minimise the unscientific factors of subjectivity and emotiveness\nMISS: exhaustion, adaptation and restoration,\nMISS: does not at all replace the entire concept of periodisation, but enriches it\nMISS: Future corroboration of the principles of periodisation may rely on some of the advances being made in the field of chronobiology.\nMISS: entrained to the cycle of day and night by nervous input from the retina,\nMISS: one from the thalamic intergeniculate structure, and another from the midbrain raphe nuclei,\nMISS: An annual plan is treated as a flexible roadmap, not a fixed contract\nMISS: in football you want to peak every Saturday\nMISS: Undulating/non-linear periodization ... is stated as the personally preferred model over strict linear progression\nMISS: non-classic\nMISS: who used the Russian concept of periodisation did not gain gold medals on Olympic games over the last 30 years, but produced great achievements before they used such concepts,\ndone","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"52526b81-638a-4247-a60b-5f5f9a94b30d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:40:35.074