{"parentUuid":"d5003617-5307-4b41-a9e0-d31ab77eb36e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a9f69a56-41de-4fd2-88ce-bc0e210b67cb","agentId":"aff5f77e5ff2eecdd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QzASmaft4hZ4ztUuAfMj8q","type":"tool_result","content":"staging/_renders/r2_6a_t344.txt:16:is ais much a matter of art, trial-and-error, and intuition, as it is of science, so that periodisation schemes should \n15-research into the nature of fractal, chaotic or frizzy processes in biology (see Ch 8). The organisation of training \n16:is ais much a matter of art, trial-and-error, and intuition, as it is of science, so that periodisation schemes should \n17-serve as approximate guidelines to be followed and modified by ongoing analysis of various physiological and \n- Undulating/non-linear periodization (Parker/Miller/Panariello), waving volume week to week (e.g., medium-high, medium, high, low over four weeks) is stated as the personally preferred model over strict linear progression, specifically to avoid staleness while still building tolerance for higher loads. **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1)**; was Inferred (transcript, speaker unconfirmed but first-person: \"For me personally, this is a more preferential model to use\") [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.24-26]\n- An annual plan is treated as a flexible roadmap, not a fixed contract: lay out the competition calendar, key non-training dates (holidays, exam weeks), and phase-by-phase volume/intensity waves, then adapt the route as circumstances change while still reaching the same destination. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.22-23; 2026-02-05-hp5355-class3-transcript.md pp.13-15]\n- In football the target is a peak every Saturday, with November and the postseason as the priority window. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q14): \"in football you want to peak every Saturday, but definitely throughout the month of November as you get closer to the postseason ... That's when players need to be at or near their peak as they head into the postseason and playoffs.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q14)** He did not say whether the postseason gets a distinct taper.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b11cf36d-2a6e-4ef4-b282-9d575c6c7a3f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:40:44.683Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"staging/_renders/r2_6a_t344.txt:16:is ais much a matter of art, trial-and-error, and intuition, as it is of science, so that periodisation schemes should \n15-research into the nature of fractal, chaotic or frizzy processes in biology (see Ch 8). The organisation of training \n16:is ais much a matter of art, trial-and-error, and intuition, as it is of science, so that periodisation schemes should \n17-serve as approximate guidelines to be followed and modified by ongoing analysis of various physiological and \n- Undulating/non-linear periodization (Parker/Miller/Panariello), waving volume week to week (e.g., medium-high, medium, high, low over four weeks) is stated as the personally preferred model over strict linear progression, specifically to avoid staleness while still building tolerance for higher loads. **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1)**; was Inferred (transcript, speaker unconfirmed but first-person: \"For me personally, this is a more preferential model to use\") [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.24-26]\n- An annual plan is treated as a flexible roadmap, not a fixed contract: lay out the competition calendar, key non-training dates (holidays, exam weeks), and phase-by-phase volume/intensity waves, then adapt the route as circumstances change while still reaching the same destination. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.22-23; 2026-02-05-hp5355-class3-transcript.md pp.13-15]\n- In football the target is a peak every Saturday, with November and the postseason as the priority window. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q14): \"in football you want to peak every Saturday, but definitely throughout the month of November as you get closer to the postseason ... That's when players need to be at or near their peak as they head into the postseason and playoffs.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q14)** He did not say whether the postseason gets a distinct taper.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d5003617-5307-4b41-a9e0-d31ab77eb36e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
